Sure! Below is a minimal example of an “interactive rotating card” that flips when you hover over it.  
Feel free to copy‑paste the code into an `.html` file (or add the CSS to your stylesheet) and tweak the colors, dimensions, or animation speed as you like.

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="pl">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<title>Rotating Card Demo</title>
<style>
/* ---------- 1️⃣ Basic reset & layout ---------- */
body {
    display:flex;
    justify-content:center;
    align-items:center;
    min-height:100vh;
    margin:0;
    background:#f0f2f5;
    font-family:sans-serif;
}

/* ---------- 2️⃣ Card container ---------- */
.card-wrapper {
    perspective:800px;          /* Gives depth to the 3D effect */
    width:260px;
    height:360px;
}

.card {
    width:100%;
    height:100%;
    position:relative;
    transform-style:preserve-3d;   /* Allows children to be positioned in 3D space */
    transition:transform .6s ease-in-out; /* Smooth rotation */
    cursor:pointer;
}

/* ---------- 3️⃣ Front side ---------- */
.front,
.back {
    position:absolute;
    width:100%;
    height:100%;
    backface-visibility:hidden;   /* Hides the reverse side while rotating */
    border-radius:12px;
    overflow:hidden;
    box-shadow:0 4px 15px rgba(0,0,0,.15);
}

.front {
    background:#fff;
    display:flex;
    flex-direction:column;
    align-items:center;
    justify-content:center;
    padding:20px;
    text-align:center;
}

.front h2 {
    margin:0 0 .5rem;
    color:#333;
}
.front p {
    margin:0;
    color:#777;
}

/* ---------- 4️⃣ Back side ---------- */
.back {
    background:#fafafa;
    transform:rotateY(180deg);     /* Start rotated so it's hidden initially */
    display:flex;
    flex-direction:column;
    align-items:center;
    justify-content:center;
    padding:20px;
    text-align:center;
}

.back h3 {
    margin:0 0 .5rem;
    color:#444;
}
.back p {
    margin:0;
    color:#555;
}

/* ---------- 5️⃣ Hover effect ---------- */
.card:hover {
    transform:rotateY(180deg);      /* Flip the whole card */
}
</style>
</head>

<body>
<div class="card-wrapper">
    <div class="card">
        <!-- Front -->
        <div class="front">
            <h2>Front Title</h2>
            <p>This is the front side of the card.</p>
        </div>
        <!-- Back -->
        <div class="back">
            <h3>Back Title</h3>
            <p>Here’s some more information on the back.</p>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
</body>
</html>
```

### How it works

| Step | What happens | Why |
|------|--------------|-----|
| **1** | `perspective` on the wrapper | Creates a 3D context so rotations look realistic. |
| **2** | `transform-style: preserve-3d` on the card | Keeps child elements in 3D space instead of flattening them. |
| **3** | `backface-visibility: hidden` on both sides | Prevents the backside from showing through during rotation. |
| **4** | `transform: rotateY(180deg)` on the back | Positions the back side behind the front initially. |
| **5** | `transform: rotateY(180deg)` on hover | Flips the entire card around the Y‑axis. |

#### Tweaking the animation

- Change the duration (`.6s`) to make it faster/slower.
- Use `rotateX` instead of `rotateY` if you prefer a vertical flip.
- Add `box-shadow` or gradient backgrounds to style each side differently.

Enjoy experimenting with this rotating card!
